.TH MAILSWIFTSYNC 1
.SH NAME
mailswiftsync \- local-first mailbox migration workbench
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mailswiftsync
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
MailSwiftSync plans, executes, verifies, and audits mailbox migrations. It
keeps migration state in a local durable ledger and requires preflight and
operator confirmation before live destination changes.
.PP
The application does not bundle or configure imapsync or Dovecot. Install and
qualify the selected transfer engine separately, then run a dry preflight.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B supervise STATE [POLL] [RETRIES] [WINDOW]
Run automation-safe supervision for queued and retryable work.
.TP
.B status STATE [PROJECT]
Print credential-free project status.
.TP
.B recover STATE
Inspect and recover interrupted work conservatively.
.TP
.B support-bundle STATE OUTPUT
Write a sanitized diagnostic bundle.
.TP
.B post-report-state STATE OUTPUT [PROJECT]
Write a fail-closed post-migration report from one consistent durable project
snapshot. If PROJECT is omitted, use the latest project in the ledger.
.TP
.B runbook SOURCE DESTINATION
Print provider setup guidance.
.TP
.B doctor [STATE] [--strict]
Report engine qualification, directory permissions, and host readiness.
.TP
.B headless STATE preflight|live|batch-preflight|batch-live [--acknowledge-destination-loss]
Run the durable controller without a window. A live plan that may remove
destination-only state (Dovecot mirror or imapsync --delete2) requires
.BR --acknowledge-destination-loss .
.SH EXIT STATUS
Commands exit 0 on success, 1 on failure, and 2 on a usage error.
.B headless live
exits 3 when another delta pass is required, 4 on a verification
difference, and 5 when operator attention is required.
.B doctor --strict
exits 1 when a check is blocked and 3 when imapsync is not the qualified
version.
.SH SAFETY
Use the dry preflight and review the generated execution plan before any live
run. Do not treat process exit status as proof of mailbox equality; review the
durable verification evidence and exceptions.
.SH FILES
The ledger location is selected through the application's normal state-path
configuration. Credentials are held in the operating-system keyring or
short-lived private runtime files; passwords are not stored in the ledger.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR imapsync (1),
.BR doveadm (1)
